# The IANA tzdata files the zone names are generated from, pinned.
#
# `cargo xtask tz-list` reads this file, checks backward, etcetera, version and
# LICENSE against their sha256 (reading CRLF as LF), and checks that `version`
# names the release jiff-tzdb bundles. The names themselves are jiff-tzdb's;
# these files say which of them are links, to what, and of what kind
# (backward's sections), and which are zones of their own. They come from
# tzdata's MAIN-format release tarball: the names and links IANA publishes.
# A link and its target carry the same bytes in either format, and tz-list
# checks that too.
#
# Never edit these files by hand. To update: take the four files from one
# release tarball (the one jiff-tzdb bundles), write that release, its date,
# the tarball's URL and sha256 and each file's sha256 here, run
# `cargo xtask tz-list` and `cargo xtask windows-zones`, and commit all of it
# together.

